Http 1.0

1. New TCP connection for every by default( may connection-alive header can be used?)
2. Buffering(trander-encoding: chuncked didn't exist)
3. no multi-homed websites (Host header isn't mandatory in request)


Http 1.1

  1. Each TCP connection by default is long living
  2. Streaming with chuncked transfer
  3. Pipelining ( disabled by default)
  4. Proxying & multi-homed websites

Http 2
  1. Compression for both headers and body
  2. Multiplexing multiple http requests on single connection
  3. Secure by default
  4. Protocol Negotiation during TLS (NPN/ALPN)

HTTP over QUIC(HTTP/3)

1. Replace TCP with QUIC(UDP with Congestion control)
2. All http/2 features
3. fixes TCP head of line blocking problem
